{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>But if in the field</b> etc. And if you ask: what difference is there between town and field, that Scripture divided their subject into two pericopes — here and here, their law is stoning — in that there is an opening for the litigant to distinguish and say that she did not cry out and consented, for had she cried out, they would have heard her, since there were witnesses there, as it is written 'and the man shall die,' and there is no death penalty without witnesses and warning. Rather, one may answer that there is a distinction in the case of the field versus the town. How so? If she is found in the town, she is always judged by stoning if she did not cry out. But if she cried out in the field, even if witnesses came in the middle of the intercourse and saw that she consented to the transgression, she is exempt. And so the interpretation of <b>but if in the field the man finds the girl</b> and witnesses came in the middle of the intercourse and warned him — regarding this the verse says <b>and the man shall die, he alone</b> — in any event, whether he forced or seduced, since he is an adulterer. And the girl — even if she said to the witnesses: leave him alone — the verse says: <b>do nothing</b>; she has no sin. Why? <b>For in the field he found her, alone</b>. And we may say: the girl cried out at the beginning of intercourse, and <b>there was none to save her</b>, for they were not there at the time of intercourse. But now that she said 'leave him alone,' that is because her inclination overcame her. And according to its plain sense, <b>the girl cried out</b> is like <b>and he saved the city through his wisdom</b>, which means: had they consulted him, he would have saved the city through his wisdom. So too here: had she cried out, no one would have saved her, and she feared lest he kill her. If so, it is a doubt for us whether she consented or not, and out of doubt she is not put to death, for a doubt in capital cases is decided leniently."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:57.574452366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}